bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    baremetal_no_freestanding_runtime_2026_11_15, 0, "Gap filed only (not implemented). Full hello program for *-unknown-none links fails on undefined rt_string_new_literal and rt_interp_cstr: src/runtime is hosted C and the SimpleOS kernel runtime is linked only on *-simpleos routes. Needs a freestanding pure-Simple runtime subset (allocator, rt_string_*, rt_interp_*, board putc) linked by baremetal_native_link.spl. See doc/08_tracking/bug/baremetal_no_freestanding_runtime_2026-11-15.md."
    baremetal_no_freestanding_runtime_2026_11_15, 1, "Implemented automatic freestanding crt0_<arch>.S assembly and pure-Simple bm_rt.spl/bm_rt32.spl --redefine-sym linking in src/compiler/70.backend/backend/baremetal_native_link.spl, and wrapped link_baremetal_native_v1 via native_link_without_startup_v2 in src/compiler/70.backend/backend/llvm_native_link_orchestrator.spl. Verified 10/10 examples in test/01_unit/compiler/backend/baremetal_native_link_spec.spl including real riscv64 crt0 assembly + llvm-nm + llvm-objcopy --redefine-sym + ld.lld ELF link with zero undefined symbols. Full bin/simple native-build of bm_rt.spl and QEMU/board boot remain pending Linux/QEMU host with built bin/simple."

